# HotFox UI asset-first correction rule

The current HotFox UI reconstruction is under corrective review.

Read first:

- `verification/ui_rebuild/HOTFOX_UI_CORRECTIVE_REVIEW_FAIL.md`
- `design/HOTFOX_18_PIXEL_LOCK_RECREATION_MASTER_PROMPT.txt`
- approved 18-screen reference package / MANIFEST

## Current gate

The current UI branch is NOT pixel-lock complete.

Current accepted visual score: **0/18** until actual app screenshots are captured and compared.

Never describe the UI as complete, final, pixel-perfect, visually passed, 1:1, or merge-ready while the evidence files show `NOT_CAPTURED` / `NOT_EXECUTED`.

## Owner asset package

The owner is preparing a ZIP of individually cut PNG elements from the approved UI.

When that package becomes available, it is the preferred production artwork source.

Mandatory intake:

1. extract to a dedicated asset workspace;
2. calculate SHA-256 for every PNG;
3. record width/height/color mode/alpha bounds;
4. create an asset-to-screen manifest;
5. classify every asset as `decorative`, `icon`, `background`, or `native-ui-reference-only`;
6. reject duplicated/ambiguous assets for manual review;
7. map assets only to screens where the approved reference proves they belong.

Do not silently modify the owner asset.

## Production raster prohibition

Do NOT create new production artwork by cropping a large rectangle from an approved full-screen screenshot.

Do NOT use a phone screenshot as the screen implementation.

Do NOT bake interactive UI into a bitmap.

Do NOT bake text, CTA, rows, tabs, switches, state labels, server values, subscription values, timers, ping, traffic, or system state into PNGs.

Allowed production PNGs:

- owner-supplied isolated PNG elements;
- truly isolated decorative artwork when independently exported and free of neighboring UI contamination.

## Planet / globe / orbit prohibition

ABSOLUTE NEGATIVE RULE:

**Never invent a planet. Never invent a globe. Never invent an orbit. Never generalize a space motif.**

A planet/globe/orbit/celestial horizon may exist only on an exact screen where the locked approved reference literally contains that exact element.

Never propagate it to another screen.

Resource naming such as `*_planet_generic`, `*_fox_planet_home`, or other generalized motif assets is a warning sign and must not be used as proof that the motif belongs globally.

## Fox prohibition

The fox is screen-owned artwork, not a globally insertable mascot.

- Do not add a fox where the exact reference does not show one.
- Do not remove one where the exact reference shows one.
- Do not redraw it into a different style.
- Do not use a generic fox asset across screens unless the exact same asset is demonstrably reused by the approved references.

## Reference hierarchy

For exact visual decisions:

1. exact approved screen reference;
2. owner-supplied isolated PNG for that screen;
3. measured design tokens extracted from the reference;
4. prose spec;
5. existing implementation.

A current XML/layout/resource is never allowed to overrule the exact approved reference merely because it is already implemented.

## Native UI remains native

The following must remain real Android UI/state:

- text;
- buttons;
- rows;
- navigation;
- switches;
- forms;
- installed-app list;
- server list;
- subscription state;
- timers;
- connection state;
- traffic values;
- latency;
- permission flow;
- Android-owned Always-on / Kill Switch state.

Decorative PNG assets may sit behind/around native UI but must not replace it.

## No global normalization against reference

Do not change one screen because another screen appears more consistent.

Do not normalize:

- tab labels;
- row presence;
- icon placement;
- CTA wording;
- spacing;
- decorative motifs;
- title composition;

unless the exact screen reference proves the normalized result.

Per-screen reference truth wins over aesthetic consistency assumptions.

## Exact correction loop

For EACH of 18 screens:

1. create deterministic state fixture in test/debug-only code if necessary;
2. build actual Android app;
3. launch on canonical emulator/device viewport;
4. navigate to exact state;
5. capture screenshot;
6. normalize only permitted system/dynamic regions;
7. compare against exact approved reference;
8. generate overlay + diff/heatmap;
9. record changed pixels, changed %, mean delta, max delta;
10. identify largest mismatch clusters;
11. fix geometry/type/color/artwork;
12. repeat until accepted;
13. only then mark screen PASS.

No estimated PASS.
No visual inspection-only PASS.
No golden-crop-only PASS.

## Dynamic values

Production values must remain truthful.

For visual regression only, deterministic test fixtures may provide stable values matching the reference.

Test fixture state MUST NOT leak into release behavior.

## Technical non-regression

Do not change the canonical VPN path for visual work:

`VpnService/TUN -> HEV/tun2socks -> local Xray SOCKS -> Xray outbound -> server -> Internet`

Do not weaken or bypass:

- connection truth;
- DNS protection;
- IPv6 handling;
- session epoch/race protection;
- AUTO/manual semantics;
- routing;
- Shadow;
- Autopilot;
- entitlement;
- device registry;
- notification/QS truth.

Do not build parallel fake state machines for screenshots.

## Merge gate

Visual merge gate is closed until:

- approved owner assets are integrated;
- unauthorized screenshot-derived composite crops are gone;
- no invented motif remains;
- no unapproved visual additions remain;
- 18 implementation screenshots exist;
- 18 reference comparisons exist;
- 18 diff results are executed;
- 18 screens are accepted;
- core regression checks pass.

Until then report exactly:

`HOTFOX UI PIXEL-LOCK: FAIL / INCOMPLETE`
